  "summary_en": "Sweden's 2026 national AI Strategy sets the goal of ranking among the world's top ten AI nations. It stresses regulatory simplification at EU level, sandboxes, standards, data sharing, public-sector AI, skills, computing capacity and defence uses, with responsible AI principles. It has almost no robotics-specific content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Aims for Sweden to rank among the top ten AI nations globally.",
   "Pushes for simpler EU AI rules and for AI legislation to wait until standards are in place.",
   "Supports regulatory sandboxes and AI standards as alternatives or complements to legislation.",
   "Plans an AI workshop for public administration, with foundations in 2026 and full operation by 2030.",
   "Annual review of the strategy; the Agency for Digital Government and PTS support implementation."
  ],
